<xml>
  <block type="device_ir_nec" x="30" y="30">
    <mutation uid="ir25" />
    <field name="NAME">remote</field>
    <field name="PIN">2</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">NEC-compatible receiver output D2, correct module supply and common ground. This is a demodulating IR receiver, not a bare photodiode. Library sampling uses Timer2 on ATmega168; do not also allocate that timer to audio or timer interrupts.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="serial_config" x="510" y="30">
    <field name="BAUD">115200</field>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_loop_section" x="990" y="30">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="arduino_typed_variable">
        <field name="VAR">command</field>
        <field name="TYPE">int32_t</field>
        <value name="VALUE">
          <block type="device_ir_command">
            <field name="DEVICE">ir25</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <next>
          <block type="controls_if">
            <value name="IF0">
              <block type="logic_compare">
                <field name="OP">GTE</field>
                <value name="A">
                  <block type="variables_get">
                    <field name="VAR">command</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <value name="B">
                  <block type="math_number">
                    <field name="NUM">0</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
              </block>
            </value>
            <statement name="DO0">
              <block type="serial_send">
                <field name="END">println</field>
                <value name="VALUE">
                  <block type="variables_get">
                    <field name="VAR">command</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
              </block>
            </statement>
          </block>
        </next>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">Read the next received command once into a variable. Print only valid frames; -1 means no frame. Open Monitor at 115200 and press buttons on an NEC remote. Avoid delay so new frames are handled promptly.</comment>
  </block>
</xml>
